 admitted pending refresh without starting a model turn; legacy runtime reads
 keep their previous behavior. In-flight steps retain
 their previous snapshot until they finish.
+
+### External supervision notices (local extension)
+
+`thread/notice/append` accepts exact `threadId`, stable `eventId` (ASCII, 128 bytes)
+and `text` (768 UTF-8 bytes, ending `[External supervision event EVENT_ID]`).
+It records bounded `external_supervision` model context and a replayable display
+message without starting a turn or altering the goal. The exact event id/text is
+idempotent; changing content refuses. The existing `item/completed` notification
+publishes the message to subscribed clients. `notificationPublished` is publication,
+not proof of rendering or human reading. `thread/notice/read` accepts threadId and
+eventId, returning retained notice/context proof for ambiguous-append reconciliation.
+History replay makes notices available after reconnect; no model turn is dispatched.
